---A `BaseAnimSetType` config contains data about animation sets that are used by entities.
---
---It is a collection of various animation Seqs, and additional data, for use when an entity performs common animations
---like walking or running.
---
---These config types can be found within the `config.BaseAnimSet` table:
---
---Info: A `BaseAnimSetType` is a Proxy usertype, which means it is safe to copy and store in your scripts. It cannot,
---however, be used with any persistent storage.
---
---Information available within an `BaseAnimSetType` includes:
---@class BaseAnimSetType
---@field id integer (Read-only) The ID of this config type.
---@field configName string (Read-only) The name of this config, i.e. `"HUMAN_WALK_ROPEBALANCE"`.
---@field typeName string (Read-only) The type of this config. Will always be `"BaseAnimSet"`.
---@field overlayHeight integer (Read-only) The height above the owning entity, in fine units, at which entity overlays like Headbars and Hitmarks are drawn.
